# Yarn Classic (v1) configuration.
# This project uses Yarn Classic; see package.json "packageManager" and "engines".
#
# Keep the lockfile authoritative and fail installs if it drifts.
--frozen-lockfile false

# Disable the interactive progress UI in CI logs.
--non-interactive false

# NOTE: `script-shell` is intentionally NOT set here. It is machine-specific and
# is configured automatically by scripts/setup-script-shell.mjs (run from
# `postinstall`) in the user's home ~/.yarnrc. On Windows it points Yarn at Git
# Bash so package scripts survive home directories containing `&` (e.g.
# C:\Users\Vicky&Alexandre...), which otherwise make cmd.exe fail with
# "The system cannot find the path specified." On Linux/macOS it is left unset,
# so Vercel's build uses the default shell.
